Nucleics Align
https://github.com/DanielTillett/nucleics-align

Nucleics Align is derived from seq-align by Isaac Turner
(https://github.com/noporpoise/seq-align, last commit dc41988, 2017). Isaac
Turner released seq-align into the public domain with the Unlicense
(https://unlicense.org): "This is free and unencumbered software released
into the public domain." Parts of the code here originate from seq-align;
source files that do are marked "original author: Isaac Turner".

The changes and additions made in Nucleics Align are copyright (c) 2026
Daniel Tillett and are licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License in LICENSE.

Versions before 2.0 bundled Isaac Turner's string_buffer (CC0 1.0),
seq_file and sort_r (public domain) as git submodules in libs/. Nucleics
Align 2.0 and later use none of them: the sequence reader in
src/cli/cli_seqio.c and the sort in src/lib/smith_waterman.c are their own.

The substitution matrices in scoring/ were obtained from the NCBI BLAST
matrix archive (https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/blast/matrices/); each file
credits its authors.
